 [L4] Every finite orthogonal list of nonzero vectors is linearly independent ([[thm-orthogonal-nonzero-vectors-are-linearly-independent]]).
 
+[L5] The span of a set is exactly the vectors obtained as finite linear combinations of its elements, including the empty combination. For a finite list, grouping the finitely many terms by their listed vectors gives a coefficient combination indexed by the list. Every subspace containing those vectors contains these combinations. ([[lem-span-is-the-set-of-linear-combinations]])
+
 ## Proof
 
 **Proof technique:** induction.
